WEBVTT

NOTE On-screen visual text only; this approved video has no audio track.

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:07.700
“Change the address… for order 4182.” The internal pause lasts 350 milliseconds in this example.

2
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:14.700
Closing after 250 milliseconds cuts the request before the order is identified.

3
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:23.000
VAD detects activity. End-of-turn needs evidence about the complete intent.

4
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:30.700
A short window can mistake a pause for the end. A long one can create silence.

5
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:37.700
Increasing the timeout protects this unfinished sentence, but delays an already complete “yes”.

6
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:46.000
Tune premature endings and waiting together. A lower latency number is not enough.

7
00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:53.700
Detecting the user’s speech early lets the system consider yielding the channel.

8
00:00:53.700 --> 00:01:00.700
Closing the user’s turn too early can change the meaning of the request.

9
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:09.000
Use separate start and end decisions, with a clear authority for each.

10
00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:16.700
“Uh-huh” can signal attention without asking the agent to stop speaking.

11
00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:23.700
“Wait, change the time” can require stopping the response and listening.

12
00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:32.000
Context decides: detected speech is evidence, not a universal cancellation command.

13
00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:39.700
R7 already has one played chunk, more queued chunks and more audio being generated.

14
00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:46.700
The interruption stops new output and removes pending audio from the queue.

15
00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:55.000
Keep the confirmed prefix. Do not confuse generated audio with actual playout.

16
00:01:55.700 --> 00:02:02.700
Two detectors can propose closing T12. They must not start two independent responses.

17
00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:09.700
One authority admits the closure once and assigns response R7.

18
00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:18.000
When T13 replaces the turn, late R7 audio must not reclaim the channel.

